{"pageid": 750, "title": "Bian", "revid": 1902, "categories": ["Characters", "Humans", "Children", "Archer's Peak", "Characters (SIKTC comics)"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-wikia pi-layout-default\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"title1\">Bian</h2>\n\n<figure class=\"pi-item pi-image\" data-source=\"image1\">\n\t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/6/6a/Bian.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215171259\" class=\"image image-thumbnail\" title=\"Bian\">\n\t\t<img src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/6/6a/Bian.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/268?cb=20241215171259\" srcset=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/6/6a/Bian.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/268?cb=20241215171259 1x, https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/6/6a/Bian.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/536?cb=20241215171259 2x\" class=\"pi-image-thumbnail\" data-relevant=\"1\" alt=\"Bian\" width=\"266\" height=\"500\" data-image-key=\"Bian.png\" data-image-name=\"Bian.png\" />\n\t\t\n\t</a>\n\t\n</figure>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Biographical Information</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"species\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Species</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Human</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"status\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Status</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Alive</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Relationships</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"affiliation\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Affiliation</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak</a><br /><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype children</span> <small>(formerly)</small></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"relatives\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Relatives</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Gail\" title=\"Gail\">Gail</a> <small>(adoptive mother)</small><br /><p>Unnamed father<br />Unnamed sister †<br /></p></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Appearances</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"first_appearance\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">First Appearance</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_5\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 5\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #5</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"last_appearance\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Last Appearance</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_15\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 15\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #15</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<blockquote class=\"pull-quote\">\n\t<div class=\"pull-quote&#95;&#95;text\">You wanted to <i>hurt</i> <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">the babies</span>. They weren't hurting anybody. They were just eating what <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype mother (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfbW90aGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">their <i>Momma</i></span> brought them.</div>\n\t<p style=\"text-align: right\"><cite>—Bian , <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_12\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 12\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #12</a></cite></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><b>Bian</b> is a young girl from <a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak, Wisconsin</a> who was a survivor of the 2020 <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak incident (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX2luY2lkZW50P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Archer's Peak incident</span>. Surviving an <a href=\"/wiki/Oscuratypes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Oscuratypes\">Oscuratype</a> attack by playing dead, Bian would become protective of <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype mother (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfbW90aGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">the monster's</span> <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">children</span> due to their perceived innocence. When the children started to grow and attack, Bian assisted <a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> in summoning and killing them.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span></h2>\n<p>Bian lived in <a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak</a>, Wisconsin, with her <span class=\"new\" title=\"Bian&#39;s Father (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQmlhbiUyN3NfRmF0aGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">father</span> and <span class=\"new\" title=\"Bian&#39;s Sister (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQmlhbiUyN3NfU2lzdGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">older sister</span>. Her father did not like the girls much, and it's suggested that they had not been living with him long, as Bian says she wasn't sure about this. When Bian's Sister was invited to <a href=\"/wiki/Carly_Monitz\" title=\"Carly Monitz\">Carly Monitz</a>'s sleepover, Bian was forced to go along as well so that her father wouldn't have to deal with her. At the party, <a href=\"/wiki/Tyler_Monitz\" title=\"Tyler Monitz\">Tyler Monitz</a> interrupted the girls' scary stories to talk about the monster his friend <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> supposedly saw in the ravine. Effectively frightened, the girls started spreading the story around school to prevent other children from going into the woods.\n</p><p>However, soon, children began to disappear. The more children that vanished, the more frightened Bian became, and she began believing she could see the monster in the forest.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC12&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC12-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> The monster eventually came to her house and ate her sister. Bian pretended to be dead, and the monster brought her body to its den. Bian remained there for a long time, as her father did not report either girl missing<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC5&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC5-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> and apparently skipped town soon after.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC15&#95;3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC15-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Bian watched the monster \"get big\" and give birth to <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">five baby monsters</span>, which she was not afraid of, unlike their mother. The mother would eat living children, and bring dead ones for her own babies to feast on.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC6&#95;4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC6-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Bian said this was not the babies' fault, as they were only eating what their mother brought them.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC8&#95;5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC8-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> She also later referred to the babies as \"nice,\" implying that she had positive interactions with them when their mother was away.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC12&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC12-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>When <a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Tommy_Mahoney\" title=\"Tommy Mahoney\">Tommy Mahoney</a> entered the monster's den, about a month-and-a-half into the Incident, Bian heard the adults speaking and managed to approach them from where she was hiding in the pile of children's body parts. Erica would stab Tommy Mahoney with Horde Gold, enabling him to see the monster, before passing Bian and an injured <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> to him to escape with. He would run them to a nearby car, where <a href=\"/wiki/John_Richards\" title=\"John Richards\">Officer John Richards</a> was recovering consciousness. Bian simply told him that the monster didn't eat her, and that she was cold; on the drive to the hospital, Richards promised to turn the heat on for her.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC5&#95;2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC5-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>After Bian's injuries were assessed, she was taken to the police station to be questioned. She refused to give her last name, as she liked the station better than her home. She also warned Officer Richards that moving the bodies would mean the babies would go hungry, but she could tell he didn't believe her. Staying in the waiting room with <a href=\"/wiki/Gail\" title=\"Gail\">Gail</a>, the secretary, Bian would spend her time drawing. Erica eventually approached her to ask about the babies, and Bian would tell her what she had noticed in the cave. She would also show her her drawings of the babies, and of Erica killing the mother.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC6&#95;4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC6-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>That night, Bian would ask Gail if she had ever seen a dead person. When Gail responded that she had seen her father die, Bian then asked if anything had tried to eat his body. Erica then returned with <a href=\"/wiki/Aaron_Slaughter\" title=\"Aaron Slaughter\">Aaron Slaughter</a>, and the two of them attempted to take Bian; Erica told her that she could take her drawing pad, and Bian also requested the markers, as she had never had so many colors. At that, John Richards entered with a gun drawn, telling Bian she could have all the drawing materials if she came with him. When Gail attempted to call <a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Joe Cavanaugh\">the Sheriff</a>, Aaron knocked her out, frightening and confusing Bian. Richards then told Bian that the hunters planned to use her as bait; she was indifferent to this, but more concerned about them trying to kill the baby monsters. Erica then knocked out Aaron and passed her off to Richards, telling him to hide her somewhere safe.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC8&#95;5-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC8-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Richards took Bian to his parents' house, which was empty as they were visiting his sister. Bian remained in an old room, coloring, until Erica reappeared. After Erica explained that the babies had grown up and begun to kill people, Bian became sad, saying she wanted them to stay small and nice. She then told Erica about when she had first heard about the monsters, confirming James was the manifester to the hunter. Erica left to comfort James, just as the <a href=\"/wiki/White_Mask\" title=\"White Mask\">White Masks</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Slaughter\" title=\"House of Slaughter\">House of Slaughter</a> arrived, capturing everyone in the house and bringing them to the back porch.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC12&#95;1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC12-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Bian, holding Erica's backpack, ran to her as <a href=\"/wiki/Cecilia_Slaughter\" title=\"Cecilia Slaughter\">Cecilia Slaughter</a> slit Richards's throat. Cecilia threatened to take the children to complete the ritual, but a dying Richards tried to shoot her, providing enough distraction for Erica to sneak away with the children. Bian asked if Richards was dead, and upon hearing he was, said, \"That's too bad. He let me bring all the colors.\"\n</p><p>At James's House, Erica told the children that they were going to do something dangerous and scary, but it would lure in the remaining monsters. She then had <a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a> reveal his real face to them,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC13&#95;6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC13-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> which frightened Bian. Erica then had the children play the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Game of Nowhere (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR2FtZV9vZl9Ob3doZXJlP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Game of Nowhere</span>, lying down and picturing images in their head to manifest into Octo. After James described the monster's creation, Bian began to cry, saying that he was talking about the Mama, who wasn't nice like the babies. Erica told her to imagine the monster Tyler had told her about, causing Octo to take its form. Octo called out for the monster's children, summoning them to James's yard. Erica left James to watch Bian as she killed the remnants of the litter outside.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC14&#95;7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC14-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Erica would eventually return to the house, silently dousing her head in cold water. She then called the House of Slaughter and reported the monsters dead, and asked James if she could use his shower.\n</p><p>A week later, the police were still unable to find Bian's family, and she was adopted by Gail. Her capture and her sister's death was blamed on <a href=\"/wiki/Tommy_Mahoney\" title=\"Tommy Mahoney\">Tommy Mahoney</a>. The last time Bian is seen, she is drawing on Gail's floor. \n</p><p>In his conversation with Erica, <a href=\"/wiki/The_Old_Dragon\" title=\"The Old Dragon\">the Old Dragon</a> suggested that Erica could have recruited Bian into <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">the Order of St. George</a>. An angry Erica replied that would have only happened if Bian was willing to come, and if not, she would have had to kill her.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC15&#95;3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC15-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Physical_appearance\">Physical appearance</span></h2>\n<p>Bian appears to be of Eastern Asian descent; her name suggests either Japanese or Vietnamese origin. She has short-cut black hair and green eyes. She has a gap between her front teeth, and a scar across her face, from above her right eye, moving downwards diagonally, with another scar on the bottom right of her lip. Bia is very skinny, with a long, narrow face.\n</p><p>When in the monster's cave, she is in an oversized pink tank top and light blue leggings. Upon being rescued, she is dressed in a teal hoodie, gray skirt, light blue socks, and black Mary Jane shoes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Personality\">Personality</span></h2>\n<p>Bian is very blunt and direct, as well as seemingly unaffected by death and gore;<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC5&#95;2-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC5-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> whether this is due to her abduction or a prior history of abuse is unknown. While discussing the monsters' eating habits, she said that the children were already dead, so they might as well feed the babies. She is not completely indifferent, though, as she is frightened by the <a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Slaughter\" title=\"House of Slaughter\">House of Slaughter</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a>'s demonic form and protective of the monster's children. The latter also shows her care and affection for the innocent, as she doesn't blame the terrifying creatures for what happened to her nor for eating what their mother brought them.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC8&#95;5-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC8-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> She did, however, eventually help destroy them after they started attacking other children.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC12&#95;1-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC12-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> \n</p><p>It is suggested she came from a difficult home life, as she preferred being in the police station waiting room to being at home. Possibly because of this, she is able to notice things many other people would overlook, even in stressful situations.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC6&#95;4-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC6-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> She is very clever and quick-witted, as she was able to play dead well enough to deceive the Oscuratype Mother, and then to survive in its lair for several days.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC5&#95;2-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC5-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> She enjoys art and drawing, and especially loves colored markers.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC6&#95;4-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC6-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appearances\">Appearances</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Something_Is_Killing_the_Children\"><i><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(comic_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (comic series)\">Something Is Killing the Children</a></i></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_5\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 5\">Issue #5</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_6\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 6\">Issue #6</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_8\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 8\">Issue #8</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 11\">Issue #11</a> <small>(cover art only)</small></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_12\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 12\">Issue #12</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_13\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 13\">Issue #13</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_14\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 14\">Issue #14</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_15\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 15\">Issue #15</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>\"Bian\" as a name can have multiple meanings:\n<ul><li>In Japanese, it can be formed from multiple kanji combinations. Most popularly, the <i>bi</i> can be from either 美, meaning \"beautiful,\" or 弥, meaning \"universally.\" The <i>an</i> could come from 安 (\"peace, quiet\"), 案 (\"plan\"), 杏 (\"apricot\") or 晏 (\"peaceful, quiet, clear, late in the day\").</li>\n<li>In Vietnamese, it is a name that means \"secret.\" It is, however, rarely used as a given name.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"a11e34614cb8698c31cc6f260ae48179\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11_Cover-jpg\" style=\"position: relative; height:184px; width:120px; top:0.5px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11_Cover.jpg\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 11 Cover.jpg (906 KB)\" style=\"height:184px; width:120px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e5/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11_Cover.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/120?cb=20230226173539\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 11 Cover.jpg (906 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"Bian, James and Erica on Issue #11 Cover A.\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Something Is Killing the Children 11 Cover.jpg\" data-image-key=\"Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11_Cover.jpg\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-caption=\"Bian,  and  on  Cover A.\"></noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 11 Cover.jpg (906 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" alt=\"Bian, James and Erica on Issue #11 Cover A.\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Something Is Killing the Children 11 Cover.jpg\" data-image-key=\"Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11_Cover.jpg\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-caption=\"Bian,  and  on  Cover A.\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e5/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11_Cover.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/120?cb=20230226173539\" /></a></div></div><div class=\"lightbox-caption\" style=\"width:185px;\">Bian, <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica</a> on <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_11\" title=\